      "hints": [
        "Set up the sum to infinity formula $S_\\infty = \\frac{a}{1 - r} = \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{1 - r} = \\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta}$.",
        "Cross-multiply to get $1 - r = \\cos^2\\theta \\implies r = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta = \\sin^2\\theta$.",
        "Multiply $a \\times r$ to show that the second term is $\\cos\\theta\\sin^2\\theta$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Use the sum to infinity formula for a geometric progression with first term $a = \\cos\\theta$:\n$$S_\\infty = \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{1 - r} = \\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta}$$",
        "Cross-multiply to solve for the common ratio $r$:\n$$\\cos^2\\theta = 1 - r \\implies r = 1 - \\cos^2\\theta = \\sin^2\\theta$$",
        "Calculate the second term $u_2 = ar$:\n$$u_2 = \\cos\\theta \\times \\sin^2\\theta = \\cos\\theta\\sin^2\\theta$$"
      ],
