      "hints": [
        "For $\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$, calculate $a = \\cos(\\pi/3) = 0.5$ and $r = \\sin^2(\\pi/3) = 0.75$.",
        "Apply the sum formula $S_{12} = \\frac{a(1 - r^{12})}{1 - r}$ and evaluate to 4 significant figures."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Evaluate the first term $a$ and common ratio $r$ at $\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$:\n$$a = \\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2} = 0.5$$\n$$r = \\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{3}{4} = 0.75$$",
        "Calculate the sum of the first $12$ terms using $S_n = \\frac{a(1 - r^n)}{1 - r}$:\n$$S_{12} = \\frac{0.5(1 - 0.75^{12})}{1 - 0.75} = \\frac{0.5(1 - 0.031676)}{0.25} = 2(0.968324) \\approx 1.937 \\quad (\\text{to 4 s.f.})$$"
      ],
